  "caveats": [
    "Full-city MIT graph is deliberately not generated here; equivalence is exact on bounded tests and 20-cut bounded A/B, with identical full-city initial content coverage.",
    "Typed flood scans O(total indexed capacity), plus sorting returned member IDs; it is not a hierarchical incremental optimization.",
    "Cuts are occupancy spheres, not gameplay HP/impulse/chain-impact evaluation. Unsupported cells remain in static graph until explicit departure; this run only queries them.",
    "No whole-city metadata array, render Entries, neighbor arrays, native bodies or native colliders are constructed.",
    "JS Maps retain two entries per structure cell. Terrain descriptor and source generator still have column-scale/transient allocations, reported separately."
  ]
